# Target

Lighthouse 100 in Performance, Accessibility, Best Practices and SEO, on mobile settings, measured on `npm run build && npm run preview` (never the dev server). CLS must be 0.

# Fonts

- Self-hosted Inter Variable (`@fontsource-variable/inter`), latin subset only, `font-display: swap`.
- Preload the latin woff2 in `index.html`. No Google Fonts or other font CDNs.

# Images and icons

- Icons are inline TSX SVG components (zero extra requests).
- The hero illustration is a `<img>` pointing at the optimized SVG, with explicit `width`, `height` and `alt=""` (decorative), and `decoding="async"`. Do not lazy-load it if Lighthouse reports it as the LCP element on any breakpoint.
- Optimize SVGs once with `npx svgo` (do not add it as a dependency) and commit the result.

# Animation

- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. Never animate layout properties (height, top, margin).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

# Bundle

- Single view: no route-level code splitting or `React.lazy`.
- Keep production JS under ~100KB gzip. Check the `vite build` output after adding anything.

# index.html / SEO

`<html lang="en">`, a descriptive `<title>`, `<meta name="description">`, `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">`, `<meta name="theme-color" content="#111827">`, and the logo mark as an SVG favicon.
